rrow, pointed leaflets. The lower fronds droop steeply around the crown base.", "Frond count looks lower than in reference-0 (roughly 20–25 against roughly 30–60). Frond length relative to visible trunk length is shorter than in reference-0, and the trunk takes up a larger share of the tree's height. The inventory records crown proportions as variation.", "The trunk carries only sparse, isolated knobs (the landed trunk organs). There are no epiphytes, branches or foliage on the trunk in any render.", "render-3 is heavily shaded: the left roughly 55% of the trunk is near-black, so surface detail there is only partly readable. Even so, the stub density visible on the lit edge is far below the references.", "The finish is broadly comparable to the spruce anchor's flat-shaded catalogue style. The anchor sets the finish floor only and is not used to judge morphology.", "No dead-frond skirt appears below the living crown in the renders. This is a secondary trait."], "findings": [{"observation": "Both whole renders read as a palm rosette of arching pinnate fronds, with the lowest fronds drooping below the crown base.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The fronds are fewer and shorter relative to trunk height than in reference-0, so the crown looks sparse and small on a tall, thin trunk.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "Frond count and frond length dials may still sit below the reference range. This is untested."}, {"observation": "The trunk is straight or very gently leaning, of near-constant diameter, and not wavy, in both seeds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Nothing grows on the trunk in either seed. The only surface 