ight trunk falls within the recorded lean variation.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Many pinnate fronds radiate from a single apex, and the older fronds recurve and droop so the crown reads as a rounded, shuttlecock-like shape in both seeds. Frond count and length are below reference-0, but the defining rosette character is present."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The leaflets are narrow and sharp-tipped, and the frond margins look bristly at whole-tree scale. Grouped, multi-angle insertion and rigidity cannot be resolved, and render-2 leaflets look flat and somewhat soft, so a match cannot be confirmed."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The trunk shows only a few small, widely spaced cup stubs on a smooth shaft. There is no tessellating spiral diamond lattice of wedge stubs. Only what is drawn was assessed, and the pattern is absent."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "No fibrous or husk infill is drawn. The trunk surface is smooth and flat-shaded."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "A single unbranched stem of near-constant diameter carries the crown in both seeds."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "No fruit bunches are drawn. Only reference-0 evidences this trait, and it shows a single seasonal state. The inventory still marks it core, and fn-111 is noted as not landed."}, {"trait_id": "owner-fronds-long-arching", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "The crown reads as a rosette of long, arching pinnate fronds with the lowest fronds drooping, in both seeds. Longer fronds and a higher frond count would still bring it closer to reference-0."}, {"trait_id": "owner-trunk-straight-constant", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The trunk is straight or very gently leaning, not wavy, and of near-constant diameter apart from a small basal flare."}, {"trait_id": "owner-trunk-bare", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2"], "explanation": "There are no epiphytes, branches or foliage on the trunk, only small leaf-base knobs."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-80-the-gap-loops-first-live-run","session_id":"6cabaaab-3542-4282-838d-f99c0e0f60c3","tools":["StructuredOutput"],"mcp_servers":[],"model":"claude-opus-5-5","permissionMode":"default","slash_commands":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","claude-api","workflow-authoring","run","run-skill-generator","advisor","agents","auto-mode-setup","autocompact","clear","color","compact","config","output-style","context","effort","fast","heapdump","init","mcp","import","model","__remote-workflow","workflow-launch-exec","reload-plugins","reload-skills","rename","ultrareview","security-review","usage-credits","extra-usage","usage","insights","recap","skill-doctor","goal","design-consent","design-revoke","list-agents","team-onboa